  "historyNote": "(See Revision Note #1, Revision Note #2, and Revision Note #3 at chapter heading for Env-A 1800) #14104, eff 11-1-24, EXPIRES: 11-1-34",
  "inScheme": "https://granitestate.github.io/rules/scheme",
  "notation": "Env-A 1810.03",
  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a1800.html",
  "prefLabel": "Env-A 1810.03 Asbestos-Containing Cementitious Roofing or Siding Materials",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 1810.03 Asbestos-Containing Cementitious Roofing or Siding Materials. The owner or operator who removes cementitious ACM from the side or roof of a building and does not sand, saw, grind, abrade, or otherwise treat the ACM in a manner that might create a fine dust or particles, shall comply with the following:\n\n(a) The asbestos abatement entity and workers shall be licensed and certified in accordance with Env-A 1815 and Env-A 1816;\n\n(b) The surrounding ground shall first be protected with poly drop cloths such that no ACM can come into contact with the ground;\n\n(c) Cementitious ACM shall be removed intact, to the extent possible, by prying out or cutting fasteners;\n\n(d) Cementitious ACM shall be carefully lowered to the ground, not dropped, thrown, or slid;\n\n(e) All ACM waste shall be removed, packaged, labelled, and disposed of in accordance with Env-A 1812.01(b), Env-A 1812.01(c), Env-A 1812.01(g), Env-A 1812.02 and Env-A 1812.03; and\n\n(f) All site preparation requirements specified in Env-A 1808.03(a) shall be completed.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note #1, Revision Note #2, and Revision Note #3 at chapter heading for Env-A 1800) #14104, eff 11-1-24, EXPIRES: 11-1-34",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a1800.html"
